.env
.env.moncho
vendor/*
node_modules/
build/

# Agent scratch space: ad-hoc scripts and the operator's own local state.
# Everything here is disposable by default; only keep what stays factually
# reusable, and never let it leak into a commit.
# The leading slash is required: a bare `agent/` would also hide docs/agent/.
#
# `agent/task-backlog.md` is the operator's personal backlog: it is a local
# notebook of what to pick up next, never part of the application.
#
# The streaming thinking capture (api/ollama.js, THINKING_FILE) lives here too now,
# under agent/thinking.md, so it needs no rule of its own.
/agent/

# The runner's own working directory: the generated Dockerfile and the resolved
# env, written by bin/lib/git.sh#ensure_local_excludes, which excludes it in
# .git/info/exclude for a project. This repository needs the rule too, because it is
# a workspace like any other when the runner is exercised against it.
/.moncho/

# The capture used to be written at the workspace root. Kept so an older checkout
# that still has the file stays clean until it is deleted.
thinking.md

# A text selection saved to a file by the conversation's copy gesture
# (app/clipboard-file.js). Written at the workspace root with a time-stamped name, it is
# the user's own scratch file and never part of the project — the same kind of thing as
# .moncho/ above, and ignored here as well as in a project's .git/info/exclude.
.moncho.clipboard.*
